WEBVTT

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.890
<i>When someone says, 
"Ни пуха ни пера"</i>

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.040
in Russia, you're supposed 
to reply, "К чёрту."

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.800
Ни пуха ни пера.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.280
Hey, I made the food today.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.580
I think it came out pretty good, myself.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.270
Luou, can you hear me?

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.720
К чёрту.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:26.800
<i>What does it mean?</i>

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.000
<i>It's a charm to make everything go well.</i>

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.590
<i>Probably, anyway.</i>

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.140
Act 9: "I Wanna Get Better, Too!"

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.980
<b>Sixth Day of Summer School</b>

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:13.360
Oh, you're here already?

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.280
I went to pick you up.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.800
Hey, I wanted to talk 
to you about something.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.870
Can we talk on the way home?

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.700
Wow! Luou, that's amazin'!

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.450
I think he's more flexible 
than some of the regular girls.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.660
I can't do it!

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:32.000
The splits you're starting 
from are different.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:41.510
<b>Ideal</b>

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:41.510
<b>Jumpei</b>

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:37.590
Your pelvis is tilted forward, 
so you can't bend back.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.900
And you're bending toward your back leg.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.510
Eh... Huh?

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.350
I'm saying...

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.220
Like this.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.100
And this!

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.270
Ow, ow, ow!

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.550
Don't twist your body.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.790
Bellybutton forward.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.360
Don't turn your front leg inward!

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.980
Someone hold down his front leg.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.070
Time out, time out, time out, time out!

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:56.160
You're jealous of me, right?

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.410
I stretched like this every day.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.740
<i>You</i> started off flexible.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:05.240
Right now, Yamato, Luou, and 
Misaki are in front of the mirror.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.270
All three dance at a very high level,

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.760
but Luou is the best by far.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.870
He has an uneven temper, and I'm 
worried about his willingness to learn,

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.160
but he's someone we'd 
only see once in decades.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:17.820
I think he should get the scholarship.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.390
What about Murao Jumpei?

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.030
Huh? Oh, right.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:24.280
Murao's face is so expressive.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.720
I like that.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.140
You can see when he's "on," 
and it fuels expectations.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.230
Nakamura-sensei, I'm not asking 
what you think about him.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.730
I want to know if he would be 
worthy of the scholarship.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.450
Give the scholarship to Murao?

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.280
What? Should I let go?

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.720
No... I'll do it!

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.370
Stop that at once!

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.080
He could've been injured!

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.780
Current standard practice is to use only 
your own body weight when stretching.

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:59.800
It's very dangerous to have others
 exert so much strength on you.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.680
That way is outdated.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.950
Did you learn this from your grandmother?

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:07.410
I think I understand 
why your mother, Mazuru,

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:11.060
ran away from your grandmother.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.760
She had so much talent.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.170
If only she'd been blessed 
with a good teacher...

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.940
You say it's outdated...

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.950
But I was never injured.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.400
And there's no one at Oikawa

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.700
who can dance better than me, is there?

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.830
<i>Oh, he said it out loud!</i>

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.460
I wonder about that.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:44.380
I'll come watch the afternoon 
class for a bit today.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.300
I'm looking forward to it.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:55.500
Oikawa Ayako-san's smile doesn't reach 
her eyes, and it scares the crap outta me!

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.740
I hear she treats the ones she likes
 as though they're in a stress interview.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.830
She must have her eye on you, Luou.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.060
Really? I wouldn't want that, though.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.960
I'd rather improve through praise.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.490
Anyway, what do you wanna eat?

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.470
Luou, can I talk to you?

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.320
Definitely no ramen. We've still 
got the afternoon class.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.320
I couldn't say it until now,

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:14.200
but I'm actually a fan of Mori Mazuru-san.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.240
You look just like her. 
I can't believe I couldn't tell.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.550
Your little brother's cute, too, huh?

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.380
Huh? You knew about her new 
partner and their son, right?

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.820
You couldn't have possibly missed it, right?

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.550
She even had pictures up on social media.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.360
I think he's about four.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.710
It sounds like Mazuru-san 
went through a lot,

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.560
but she seems happy now.

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.310
You aren't goin' to live with her?

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:43.500
Lies.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.080
Huh?

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:48.570
She just makes it look like she's happy.

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:51.840
That woman's a dirty liar.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.290
I don't want anything more to do with her.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.990
Well, I guess that didn't work...

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.560
Your dancing is dynamic, 
with consistent technique.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.180
Your smile is cute, too.

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:18.690
But your connecting movements are sloppy.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.040
You're not graceful enough for a prince.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:25.070
Instead of seeing <i>Swan Lake</i>, 
I see a Shiga lake.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.730
What?! You mean Lake Biwa?!

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.910
You boys are dancing 
the part of Prince Siegfried.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.380
Grace over quirkiness.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.380
Elegance over vigor.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:37.560
On the last day,

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:42.160
please take me to the world of <i>Swan Lake</i>.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.090
<i>It's completely different 
from what Chizuru-san said.</i>

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.520
Next.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.520
Luou.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.010
<i>Ни пуха ни пера.</i>

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.010
<b><i></i></b>I pray for your success.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.100
К чёрту.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:58.800
<b><i></i></b>To the devil!

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:04.220
Luou, I'll definitely come back for you!

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:07.800
If you start missing me, 
just say this charm.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.590
Even if we're apart, I'll answer you!

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.700
Luou, what's wrong?

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:42.190
Luou?

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.440
If you're not going to 
perform, then move back.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.440
You're in the way.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:55.860
Luou!

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.360
Leave him.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.230
Luou!

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.400
What're you doing? Don't leave!

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.010
Is it what he said about your mom?

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.260
No!

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:14.470
It's because there's nothing 
for me to learn here!

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.470
Or from Chizuru-san, either!

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:20.060
That's why I wanted to go overseas!

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.230
But I don't care about that anymore, either.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:27.730
So what if I can do ballet?

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.160
You idiot! What's your deal?!

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:33.610
Don't you like doing ballet?

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.760
No, I hate it!

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:36.580
I was just forced to do it!

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.410
What?!

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:45.700
Liar! You <i>do</i> like ballet!

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.470
We're done!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.710
Jumpei-kun.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.960
Ayako-san requested that 
you come to the office.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:59.590
Oh, crap! Is she gonna tell
 me to quit showing up?

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:03.160
She didn't have any comments 
for me earlier, either.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.420
I wonder.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.350
<b><b>Office</b></b>

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:13.110
<b><b>Office</b></b>

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.110
Excuse me.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.780
You were summoned by Ayako-san?

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.510
Is it because of me and Luou?

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.120
Oh, no.

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:27.870
It was about me. About what I'm thinking...

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:33.690
Oh, I heard Luou left 
in the middle of class?

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:38.960
To Luou, Grandma's word is absolute,

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:44.890
and she rejected Japanese ballet because 
she thought Russia was the best.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:48.400
I thought maybe you'd 
helped him change a little,

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:50.770
but I guess it's not that easy.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.150
I'll go pick up Luou tomorrow morning.

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:58.040
Hey...

00:09:58.460 --> 00:09:59.400
Let's go somewhere!

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:00.100
Huh?

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:02.270
It's summer vacation... The last day!

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:06.000
After the summer school variation 
performances, let's go somewhere...

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.000
The two of us!

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:10.040
Yeah!

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.750
<i>Yeah! I like her!</i>

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.570
<i>Cutest in the world. Cutest in the world.</i>

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.680
<i>Cutest in the world. Cutest in the world.</i>

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.140
It's Murao. Excuse me...

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.650
<i>Is this the </i>Romeo and Juliet<i> 
from the other day?</i>

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:31.520
Reverence!

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:46.970
Well, Murao Jumpei-kun? 
How have the last six days been?

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:49.240
Your world has changed 
considerably, has it not?

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:53.230
Your dancing and attitude 
are completely different.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:56.270
You wouldn't have changed 
that much without trying.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:00.430
I'll get straight to the point.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:06.180
I'm thinking of giving you 
the scholarship to the SS class.

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:11.310
Every year, we keep one spot open 
for a student from the summer school.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.690
I'd like to know if you are interested.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:16.830
<i>C-Crap...</i>

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:18.370
<i>I'm really happy!</i>

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.680
If you get the scholarship,

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:24.200
it's proof that I've acknowledged you, right?

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.450
U-Um, but why?

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:28.960
Why me?

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.570
I mean, Luou is way better than me.

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:36.390
That's true. He's already quite skilled,

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:39.700
and his performances 
miraculously draw people in.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:40.470
However,

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.180
he cannot become a professional.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:47.620
To leave class just because 
he was shaken by something...

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:50.090
He's too mentally weak. 
He can't get along with others.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:51.810
He has no common sense.

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.440
Above all,

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.430
no matter how talented someone is,

00:11:56.430 --> 00:12:00.940
if they don't <i>want</i> to learn, 
there's nothing we can do here.

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:05.780
Don't tell me Chizuru-san also told you

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:09.270
that you had to be the best in Russia?

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:13.520
It's not that she said I "had" 
to be. I'm the one who—

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.880
I see. What made you say that?

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.710
I just thought... it'd be cool...

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.080
to be the best in Russia, or something...

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:24.900
I see. I understand.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:28.040
Will you listen to what 
I'm aiming for, as well?

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:32.320
I want to raise the status of 
the Japanese ballet world.

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:38.860
Up to heights that will drive overseas 
dancers to want to join Oikawa.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:43.170
To accomplish that, 
many things need to be done.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:47.330
Salaries and guarantees for dancers, 
the repertoire, sponsors,

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:50.380
and even perhaps cultivating 
the audience for ballets.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:56.750
And a star dancer who will become 
the target of absolute adoration is essential.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:00.400
A principal who will make ballet history...

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:03.470
It'd be even better if they 
were trained by Oikawa, too.

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:06.280
That's what I want you to become.

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:10.970
Don't you think that's even 
more preposterous and interesting

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.400
than aiming to be a top Russian dancer?

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:22.730
<i>So, here are the conditions for 
awarding you the scholarship.</i>

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:26.320
<i>You will eventually join the Oikawa company,</i>

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:28.590
<i>and stop attending 
the Godai Ballet Studio.</i>

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:32.420
<i>If you cannot accept those conditions 
and do not want the scholarship,</i>

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:37.960
<b>Godai Ballet Studio</b>

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:39.460
<i>then please do not come 
to the variation performances</i>

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.320
<i>on the last day of summer school.</i>

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:44.970
Chizuru-san, I...

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.090
I was acknowledged by Ayako-san!

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:49.850
Now the little kids will come back, too!

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:53.890
What, are you planning on accepting 
the scholarship for the SS class?

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:54.720
You're sharp!

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:58.110
I thought I'd go to both schools!

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:01.940
You can't do that.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:04.770
That doesn't sound like something 
Ayako-san would allow.

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:05.960
It's against the rules.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.000
What about becoming a top dancer in Russia?

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:12.690
If you accept the scholarship, you will 
be expected to join Oikawa eventually.

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:18.130
Yeah, but it sounds like they have an 
overseas study abroad training program,

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:21.920
so I thought I'd take the chance if 
I could get it. Like you, Chizuru-san!

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:24.150
Ayako-san told me.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:27.560
Even though you were studying under 
the previous artistic director, Oikawa Haruka,

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:29.530
you went to study abroad in Russia, right?

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:31.500
You got prestige for dancing in Russia,

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.430
then came back to Oikawa 
and joined the company,

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.880
so I could return the favor the same way—

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:35.440
Idiot!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:39.280
The ballet world is more 
connected than you think.

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:42.470
A bad reputation will stay with you 
as long as you're still dancing.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:46.990
And nothing will suppress 
the shine of a dancer on the rise.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.860
I wasn't able to return the favor at all.

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:52.970
And now that Haruka-san is gone,

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:55.690
it's something that will stay 
with me for the rest of my life.

00:14:57.110 --> 00:14:59.360
Then... going to Russia...

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.060
I don't regret it.

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:04.530
I wanted to go. I can't help that.

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:07.010
I'm saying you can't go into it knowing
 you won't fulfill the condition.

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:10.720
Chizuru-san, you really 
think outside the box, huh?

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:14.140
You didn't get mad at the ballet 
festival, either. Unlike Ayako-san.

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:15.900
What was there to be mad about?

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:17.900
It was truly fun to watch.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:23.520
That makes me so happy.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:25.740
But...

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:32.140
I feel like someone like me can't just stay
in a place that accepts that part of me.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:36.110
Going to a place as strict as 
Oikawa made me think that.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:39.300
That's why I thought maybe I'd go to both—

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:40.370
Very well!

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:43.210
Don't show your face here anymore.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:46.530
Putting aside the rules,

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:48.770
if you don't think being here 
is helping you anymore,

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:51.800
and you can't do what I say 
and trust me 100%,

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:54.800
then we can't work together anymore.

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:58.710
Goodbye, then. Do your best at Oikawa.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.090
You're kidding, right?

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:07.660
If that's the case, I'll stay at Godai!

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:09.900
I won't take the scholarship at Oikawa!

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:12.580
Chizuru-san!

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:20.620
<i>I'll find a good time to talk to her.</i>

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:26.380
<i>But today's only the seventh day of 
summer school, a regular lesson day.</i>

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:30.380
<b>Seventh Day of Summer School</b>

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:29.890
<i>It's okay for me to go to Oikawa, right?</i>

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.650
What?! Me, in front of the mirror?!

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:34.670
What?!

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:41.270
<i>But Luou's the best.</i>

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:44.140
<i>He cannot become a professional.</i>

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:48.840
The curse on that boy isn't
 something that is easily broken.

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:52.180
<i>That's not right!</i>

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:54.740
<i>I can't believe she doesn't acknowledge him!</i>

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.390
<i>How can that curse be broken?</i>

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:00.490
<b>Boys' Changing Room</b>

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.680
Tomorrow's the last day, huh?

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:05.420
It felt long, but also went by so fast...

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.230
It's too early for nostalgia!

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:10.130
There's still the big climax: 
the variation performances!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:13.670
Jumpei, are ya comin' tomorrow?

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:18.350
You came to get revenge for the
 criticism about Godai-sensei, right?

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:21.940
Does Godai-san even want ya to do that?

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.500
Yeah, you're right.

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:28.070
It'd make sense not to show up tomorrow.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:33.110
But I kinda want the scholarship now!

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.470
Sorry!

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:40.530
What the hell?

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.930
What do you mean, you "kinda" want it?!

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:46.380
I've been workin' toward this 
scholarship for the past <i>year.</i>

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:49.790
It was my only hope for continuin' with ballet.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.920
Who the hell do you think you are, 
just wanderin' in like that and...

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.930
I understand how Luou feels!

00:17:56.930 --> 00:18:01.220
Did ya even realize
 Luou likes Miyako-chan?

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:04.060
You two kissed, didn't ya? What a joke!

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:06.570
Luou saw it, too!

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:07.660
You're so damn oblivious!

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:10.450
You don't even<i> try</i> to see 
how other people feel!

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:10.450
Hey!

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:14.400
You just waltz in and take 
the best part for yourself!

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.660
Misaki, what's wrong? This isn't like ya!

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:21.500
I...

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:24.040
I've liked ballet for eight years.

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.560
What's that got to do with it?

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:27.650
I always,

00:18:27.650 --> 00:18:29.420
<i>always</i> wanted to do it!

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:33.880
It was my own fault for not having 
the courage to go to lessons.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:36.260
But I danced in my own way in secret,

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:40.640
and now, I'm finally learning real ballet!

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:42.010
I...

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.520
I wanna get better, too!

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:50.540
<i>That's all...</i>

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.150
<i>That's all there is to it. 
What's wrong with that?</i>

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.440
<i>I want Chizuru-san to teach me.</i>

00:18:58.240 --> 00:18:59.150
<i>But...</i>

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:02.990
<i>in order...</i>

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:05.870
<i>to get better...</i>

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:35.900
<i>If I'm... at Oikawa...</i>

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.760
Jumpei!

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:45.280
I'm glad... I caught you!

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:48.910
Look, I grabbed a bunch of movie flyers.

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:50.670
You like movies, right?

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:54.480
I thought it'd be nice to get an After 5 
ticket for an amusement park, too,

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:56.410
but we'd only be there for a couple of hours.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:58.300
Oh, you mean tomorrow?

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:01.060
<i>I can't believe it...</i>

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:04.570
<i>She's super excited about it!</i>

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.930
<i>I've decided. I'll stay at Godai!</i>

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:12.250
<i>Yeah, I mean, Chizuru-san 
focuses on the basics like Oikawa.</i>

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:16.190
<i>Besides, there's no one at Oikawa 
who's better than Luou.</i>

00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:18.650
He cannot become a professional.

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:24.660
Huh?

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:28.370
I said, I'm not going to today's 
variation performances,

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:29.660
so let's go to an amusement park!

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.960
What? No, you have to perform.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:34.330
You worked so hard this past week.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:37.380
Your dancing's changed in a good way!

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:41.880
Yeah... I'm grateful to Ayako-san...

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:43.050
But I'm not going.

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:44.220
That said...

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:45.610
I'm comin' in!

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:46.970
Wha—

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:49.970
Luou! You're in there, right?

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:53.800
Right now, Miyako and I are going 
on somethin' like a date—

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:55.230
No, it <i>is</i> a date!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:57.230
It's definitely, <i>totally</i> a date!

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:01.620
Are you stupid? You... I mean, 
she's such a c-c-c-cute girl!

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:03.480
Right under your nose, too...

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:06.240
It's a <i>huge</i> turn of events! Idiot! Dumbass!

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:08.770
It's 'cause you just stay locked up in there!

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:12.410
That's why Ayako-san says 
you can't become a pro!

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:14.250
Doesn't that piss you off?!

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:17.420
C'mon, you gotta go to 
the variation performances!

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:20.580
While I'm enjoying the springtime of life,

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:24.070
you should go show Ayako-san 
just how good you are!

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:28.130
Make her feel like you're someone 
who needs to be shown to the world!

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:29.830
Make her eat her damn words!

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:31.070
C'mon!

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:36.270
If you don't, then it'll piss <i>me</i> off!

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:39.550
Hey! Are you listeni—

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:42.430
It's unlocked...

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:45.240
Luou?

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:21.000
<b><i>Preview</i></b>

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:26.000
The only warmth Luou ever knew 
was Miyako. She was his light.

00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:33.240
<i>Dance Dance Danseur</i>, Act 10: 
"Miyako... Needs to Be by His Side."

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:35.480
Act 10
 "Miyako... Needs to Be by His Side"
